{"path":"coroutine/generator/promise_type/operator_new","title":"std::generator<Ref,V,Allocator>::promise_type::operator new","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">generator&lt;Ref,V,Allocator&gt;::promise_type::</span>operator new","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/coroutine/generator/promise_type/operator_new","section":"coroutine","kind":"page","summary":"Allocates size bytes of uninitialized storage using default or user-provided allocator.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/operator_new\"><span class=\"kw692\">operator new</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> size <span class=\"br0\">)</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/same_as\"><span class=\"kw2951\">std::<span class=\"me2\">same_as</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Allocator, <span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/default_initializable\"><span class=\"kw2965\">std::<span class=\"me2\">default_initializable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Allocator<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td><div><span id=\"Version_2\"></span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Alloc, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span>... <span class=\"me1\">Args</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/operator_new\"><span class=\"kw692\">operator new</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> size, <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_arg\"><span class=\"kw706\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator_arg_t</span></span></a>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Alloc<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> alloc, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Args<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>... <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2)</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> This, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Alloc, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span>... <span class=\"me1\">Args</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/operator_new\"><span class=\"kw692\">operator new</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> size, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> This<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_arg\"><span class=\"kw706\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator_arg_t</span></span></a>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Alloc<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> alloc, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Args<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>... <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/coroutines#Dynamic_allocation\">Allocates</a> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">size</span></code> bytes of uninitialized storage using default or user-provided allocator.\n</p><p>Let <code>A</code> be\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code>Allocator</code>, if it is not <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span></span>,\n</li><li> <code>Alloc</code> for <span class=\"t-v\">(2,3)</span>, or\n</li><li> <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator\"><span class=\"kw704\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> otherwise.\n</li></ul>\n<p>Let <code>B</code> be <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits\"><span class=\"kw705\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator_traits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>A<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"kw1\">template</span> rebind_alloc<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> where <code>U</code> is an unspecified type whose size and alignment are both <a href=\"/w/cpp/preprocessor/replace#Predefined_macros\"><code>__STDCPP_DEFAULT_NEW_ALIGNMENT__</code></a>.\n</p><p>Initializes an allocator <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> of type <code>B</code> with:\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">A<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>,</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2,3)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">A<span class=\"br0\">(</span>alloc<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>Uses <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> to allocate storage for the smallest array of <code>U</code> sufficient to provide storage for a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/coroutines#Execution\">coroutine state</a> of size <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">size</span></code>, and unspecified additional state necessary to ensure that <a href=\"/w/cpp/coroutine/generator/promise_type/operator_delete\"><code>operator delete</code></a> can later deallocate this memory block with an allocator equal to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code>.\n</p><p>The program is ill-formed unless <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits\"><span class=\"kw705\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator_traits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>B<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">pointer</span></span> is a pointer type and for overloads <span class=\"t-v\">(<a href=\"#Version_2\">2,3</a>)</span>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/same_as\"><span class=\"kw2951\">std::<span class=\"me2\">same_as</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Allocator, <span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/convertible_to\"><span class=\"kw2953\">std::<span class=\"me2\">convertible_to</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Alloc<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>, Allocator<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is modeled.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> size\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the size of the storage to allocate\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> alloc\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a user provided allocator of type <code>Alloc</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A pointer to the allocated storage.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> May throw.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3900\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3900</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++23\n</td>\n<td>overloads <span class=\"t-v\">(<a href=\"#Version_2\">2,3</a>)</span> were constrained on conversion of <code>Alloc</code> to <code>Allocator</code>\n</td>\n<td>mandated\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"coroutine","title":"Coroutine support (C++20)"},{"path":"coroutine/generator","title":"std::generator"},{"path":"coroutine/generator/promise_type","title":"std::generator<Ref,V,Allocator>::promise_type"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::generator<Ref,V,Allocator>::promise_type::operator new","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Allocates size bytes of uninitialized storage using default or user-provided allocator."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"size, alloc"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A pointer to the allocated storage."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw."}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":248,"codeBlockCount":0}
